A prose paragraph, focused
description: the chapter_prose_editing state
- >
  A body paragraph as the shared marklower editor. Enter makes a SIBLING paragraph (THE PROSE
  EXCEPTION), not a descent. An EMPTY chapter shows one bootstrap paragraph (no entry until the
  first typed text - merely opening writes nothing) - and the bootstrap is NOT an idle state; a
  format command MATERIALIZES the first entry of that kind (a one-cell table in its creation flow,
  a one-item list, an empty paragraph), T makes an empty title to type into, D an empty
  description
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`enter`', 'split at the caret; the tail is a new sibling paragraph', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`ctrl_enter`', 'outside a table - THE TABLE GESTURE: the paragraph wraps as a one-cell table in its creation flow (Tab grows columns, Ctrl+Enter then appends rows); on the bootstrap paragraph the table MATERIALIZES as the first entry', '[format_switched](::server:chapter-editor:format_switched)']
  - ['`ctrl_enter`', 'inside a table cell''s inner chunks - appendRow - the gesture stays one gesture', '[table_cell_editing](::server:chapter-editor:table_cell_editing)']
  - ['`tab`', 'any paragraph NESTS - it becomes the sole paragraph of a fresh UNTITLED group (`- x` -> `- - x`, one replace op), STAYING a paragraph one level deeper. The title role is EXPLICIT: T titles the group (and the group materializes in a dir chapter once it is titled with body). The group carries the session wrap badge', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', 'below the root level - lift it out of its subchapter', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', 'otherwise', '[nop](::server:yamlover-editor:nop)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the caret is at the start - joinPrev - WALK-ADJACENT: into the previous walk cell (a paragraph merges; a subchapter TITLE dissolves in title-text-first, the chapter''s OWN heading included - the chapter flattens around the caret; a MATERIALIZED subchapter rings); description/table/atom partners RING', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise - native contentEditable editing', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`delete`', 'the caret is at the end - joinNext - WALK-ADJACENT: pulls the next walk cell in (a following subchapter''s TITLE dissolves, its body splicing out; an emptied untitled group husk-removes)', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`delete`', 'otherwise - native', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`ctrl_alt_number`', '', '[format_switched](::server:chapter-editor:format_switched)']
  - ['`role_button`', 'T / D makes THIS chunk the chapter''s title / description (only offered where the chapter lacks one)', '[chapter_title_editing](::server:chapter-editor:chapter_title_editing)']
  - ['`up_down_arrow`', 'at the first/last visual line, the caret walks to the adjacent cell', '`chapter_prose_editing` (stays)']
